.SH FUNCTIONALITY
.LP
When called, '\fB²DPROG²\fR' accomplishes the following:
.LP
\fB1)\fR General and program-specific defaults are set (directories, host, minute sequence).
.LP
\fB2)\fR Defaults are loaded from the configuration file, if it exists (default: \fB²DPROG².conf\fR in the program directory).
.LP
\fB3)\fR Command line arguments are evaluated.
.LP
\fB4)\fR If \fB-shdr\fR is set: the waiting, faxed and notfaxed directory paths are printed to \fBstdout\fR and the program exits. This option is used by \fBautofax\fR to determine the spool directories at runtime.
.LP
\fB5)\fR The three spool directories are checked and created if needed.
.LP
\fB6)\fR If \fB-fl\fR and \fB-to\fR are given (queue a fax):
.br
\fBa)\fR A TIFF file is copied directly to the waiting directory.
.br
\fBb)\fR A PDF file is first converted to TIFF format (Group 4, A4, 204x196 dpi) using \fBgs\fR (Ghostscript).
.br
\fBc)\fR A sequentially numbered control file \fBdtN.vw\fR is created. It contains: the current timestamp, the minute sequence for send retries, the target number, the source file path and the total number of send attempts. The program also enters itself into crontab if needed.
.br
\fBd)\fR The name of the control file is printed to \fBstdout\fR.
.LP
\fB7)\fR If \fB-oi\fR (only insert) is set, the program exits after queuing without attempting to send.
.LP
\fB8)\fR Regular run (queue processing): the program searches the waiting directory for control files \fBdt*.vw\fR with a corresponding non-empty TIFF file. For each file it checks whether the next send time (stored start time plus next minute from the minute sequence) has been reached. If so:
.br
\fBa)\fR The page count of the TIFF file is determined and the timeout calculated accordingly (one minute per page plus connection setup).
.br
\fBb)\fR The program forks a child process that calls \fBdmain()\fR. \fBdmain()\fR establishes a connection to the Fritz!Box via the TR-064 protocol (SOAP requests via \fBlibcurl\fR) and submits the TIFF file for fax transmission.
.br
\fBc)\fR The parent process waits up to \fBmaxsec\fR seconds for the child. On timeout the child is terminated.
.LP
\fB9)\fR Depending on the result of the send attempt, the files are moved to the faxed or notfaxed directory, or the next entry in the minute sequence is noted for the next retry.
.LP
\fB10)\fR The configuration file is written if necessary.
.SH CONTROL FILE FORMAT
Each control file \fBdtN.vw\fR contains line by line:
.LP
\fBLine 1:\fR Unix timestamp of the start time (or last attempt)
.br
\fBLine 2:\fR remaining minute sequence, comma-separated (e.g. \fB0,2,3,5,10\fR); the first value gives the minutes until the next attempt
.br
\fBLine 3:\fR target fax number
.br
\fBLine 4:\fR path of the source file
.br
\fBLine 5:\fR attempts made/total attempts (e.g. \fB2/16\fR)
.SH PRECONDITIONS
\fBHardware\fR: Fritz!Box with active fax function (fax must be configured in the Fritz!Box web interface), reachable in the local network under the configured host (default: \fBfritz.box\fR).
.br
\fBSoftware\fR: Linux (Opensuse >= 42.1, Debian >= 9, Ubuntu >= 16.04, Mint >= 18, Fedora >= 24). \fBlibcurl\fR must be installed. \fBghostscript\fR (\fBgs\fR) is needed for PDF faxing. \fBlibtiff\fR must be installed.
